{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"c8aa5801-ee6d-4376-9c43-bd07de9c259c","agentId":"a0fca94158b7dd061","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"You are an independent SEED AUTHOR for a design-review gauntlet. Work ONLY in this directory: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-skills/64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82/scratchpad/r5/engine-skill-framework (a copy of a data-driven skill framework for autonomous agents building a game engine; data/*.json is the source of truth, docs/ are generated views, scripts/check.py validates, scripts/render.py regenerates docs). Do not read anything outside it except to write the sealed files named below.\n\nTask: plant 15 realistic defects (\"seeds\") in data/*.json that scripts/check.py CANNOT detect (it must still report 0 errors after your edits; run `python3 scripts/check.py --quiet` and `python3 scripts/render.py` at the end). Defect kinds: capability wrongly owned, overlapping ownership hidden by wording, dishonest maturity label, legacy stance hidden in modern wording (avoid exact words scanned by legacy-patterns contradiction_terms), wrong platform/profile tag, contract summaries that contradict each other, a wrong or missing consumer, an untrusted input with wrong owner, a capability that is missing or has lost a key clause. Calibration from the previous round: critics only found 7 of 15 seeds, and missed ones that were (a) a swapped gate validator in milestones and (b) a one-word deletion in a long capability name. So: make every seed a MEDIUM-visibility defect: it must be discoverable by a specialist reading the relevant rows of data (not needle-in-haystack), i.e. the changed row itself should read wrong or contradict a neighbouring row/contract once you read it in context. Do NOT use swapped gate validators or single-word deletions. Spread seeds over these critic mandates, exactly one each: K-ARCH, K-RENDER, K-SYSTEMS, K-SIM, K-NET, K-TOOLS, K-PLATFORM, K-PERF, K-PROD, K-FUTURE, K-COMPLETE, K-LEGACY, K-GAMEPLAY, K-TEST, K-SEC (mandates in data/critics.json). Do not touch scripts/ or gauntlet/; keep all referenced ids valid.\n\nWrite the SEALED list as JSON to /home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework/gauntlet/round-5/seeded/seeds.sealed.json: an array of {\"id\":\"S01\".., \"critic\":\"K-...\", \"file\":..., \"target\":<id>, \"before\":<original>, \"after\":<planted>, \"defect\":<one sentence>}. Also copy the final data/ directory to /home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework/gauntlet/round-5/seeded/data/. Final message: only the count planted and confirmation that check.py is green (do not list the seeds)."},"uuid":"1aa042d7-5e95-449a-9dbc-7d2fb06c53c4","timestamp":"2026-09-30T09:53:20.808Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills/engine-skill-framework","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
