time-architect | E | ['editor-architect', 'crash-diagnostics', 'security-engineering']\nCORE.LIFE.config-snapshots | Config reads via immutable snapshots latched at sync points; queued change notification | core-runtime-architect | E | ['frame-orchestration']\nCORE.LIFE.interop | Multi-language interop & memory-safe components (FFI/ABI rules, ownership across boundaries) | core-runtime-architect | M | ['security-engineering', 'build-system-toolchains']\nCORE.LIFE.config-trust | Config trust tiers per layer & per-cvar settable-from allow-lists (no code loading or path cvars from command-line, intent or remote layers in shipping) | core-runtime-architect | E | ['security-engineering']\nCORE.MATH.linear | SIMD linear algebra (vectors, matrices, quaternions) | math-simd-numerics | E\nCORE.MATH.geometry | Geometry primitives & intersection tests | math-simd-numerics | E\nCORE.MATH.compgeo | Computational geometry (hulls, triangulation, booleans) | math-simd-numerics | E\nCORE.MATH.robustness | Numerical robustness & precision analysis | math-simd-numerics | E\nCORE.MATH.precision | Double & mixed-precision math for large worlds | math-simd-numerics | E | ['spatial-transforms']\nCORE.MATH.deterministic | Cross-platform reproducible math library | math-simd-numerics | M | ['determinism-replay']\nCORE.MATH.random | Random numbers (counter-based / per-stream for parallel determinism) & noise | math-simd-numerics | E\nCORE.MATH.curves | Curves, splines & interpolation | math-simd-numerics | E\nCORE.MATH.spmd | Wide-SIMD / SPMD kernels for fixed and scalable (VLA) vector ISAs, runtime ISA dispatch | math-simd-numerics | E | ['cpu-performance']\nCORE.MATH.formats | Half, packed & quantized numeric formats | math-simd-numerics | E\nCORE.MATH.bignum | Large-magnitude/arbitrary-precision numeric types with canonical serialization | math-simd-numerics | E\nCORE.MATH.fixed-point | Fixed-point numerics for cross-platform lockstep and rollback | math-simd-numerics | E | ['determinism-replay']\nCORE.MEM.virtual | Virtual memory reservation, mapping & page-size policy (4K/64K/2M, large/huge pages, commit/decommit granularity per platform, client and server) | memory-allocators | E\nCORE.MEM.allocators | Allocator family with scoped arenas: reset keyed to a completion token or frame-in-flight slot (C-LIFETIME), pools, thread caches | memory-allocators | E\nCORE.MEM.thread-caches | Thread-local caches & NUMA-aware allocation | memory-allocators | E\nCORE.MEM.tracking | Memory tagging, tracking & attribution | memory-allocators | E | ['observability-telemetry']\nCORE.MEM.budget-enforcement | Budget enforcement mechanisms per subsystem | memory-allocators | E | ['performance-architect']\nCORE.MEM.fragmentation | Fragmentation control & defragmentation/relocation | memory-allocators | E\nCORE.MEM.debugging | Memory debugging (guard pages, poisoning, sanitizer integration) | memory-allocators | E | ['robustness-fuzzing']\nCORE.MEM.oom | Out-of-memory policy & graceful degradation | memory-allocators | E\nCORE.MEM.uma | Unified-memory CPU/GPU accounting, reported into RES.MGMT.arbitration (no independent arbitration) | memory-allocators | E | ['gpu-memory-resources']\nCORE.MEM.field-detection | Field detection of heap corruption in shipping builds: sampled guard allocator (E) and hardware memory-tagging mode (M), overhead budgets in C-BUDGET | memory-allocators | E | ['crash-diagnostics', 'security-engineering']\nCORE.TYPES.containers | Containers (arrays, open-addressing hash maps, inline, SoA, intrusive, rings) | containers-core-types | E\nCORE.TYPES.strings | Strings, UTF-8 handling, interned names | containers-core-types | E\nCORE.TYPES.hashing | Non-cryptographic & stable content hashing with versioned algorithm/seed guarantees | containers-core-types | E\nCORE.TYPES.bits | Bit manipulation & bitsets | containers-core-types | E\nCORE.TYPES.algorithms | Sort, search & generic algorithms | containers-core-types | E\nCORE.TYPES.ownership | Span/view & explicit-ownership types | containers-core-types | E | ['core-runtime-architect']\nCORE.TYPES.codecs | Compression codec library for all users (package and non-package): vetted zstd/LZ4/Kraken-class decoders, SIMD tuning, fuzz registration | containers-core-types | E | ['package-formats-vfs']\nCORE.TYPES.crypto | Vetted cryptographic primitives wrapper, CSPRNG, per-platform selection | security-runtime | E | ['security-engineering', 'containers-core-types']\nCORE.TYPES.hash-dos | Keyed hashing (SipHash class) mandated for containers keyed by untrusted data | containers-core-types | E | ['security-engineering']\nCORE.CONC.atomics | Memory model & atomics | concurrency-primitives | E\nCORE.CONC.sync | Synchronization primitives (futex-backed locks, events, spin with backoff); no subsystem-wide locks on frame paths; priority inheritance/donation where the OS offers it, no spinning across QoS classes, lock-class registry (frame-critical, RT-forbidden) | concurrency-primitives | E\nCORE.CONC.lockfree | Lock-free / wait-free structures (MPMC queues, work-stealing deques) | concurrency-primitives | E\nCORE.CONC.reclamation | Safe memory reclamation (epochs, hazard pointers) | concurrency-primitives | E\nCORE.CONC.correctness | Thread-safety annotations and model-checking hooks (litmus/linearizability reference scenes and threshold proposals only; suite authorship belongs to the contract's oracle_author) | concurrency-primitives | E | ['robustness-fuzzing']\nCORE.CONC.retirement | Retirement service (C-LIFETIME): completion-token, fence and epoch retire queues shared with safe memory reclamation | concurrency-primitives | E | ['core-runtime-architect', 'rhi-core', 'gpu-memory-resources']\nCORE.CONC.layout | Cross-thread data layout: per-target destructive-interference size, padding and sharding rules, per-worker sharded counters and queues, padding lint | concurrency-primitives | E | ['containers-core-types', 'platform-architect']\nCORE.JOBS.scheduler | Work-stealing job scheduler | job-system-task-graph | E\nCORE.JOBS.graph | Task graphs with explicit dependencies | job-system-task-graph | E\nCORE.JOBS.fibers | Fibers & language coroutines (fiber-safe TLS, debugger/profiler/sanitizer annotations) | job-system-task-graph | E | ['crash-diagnostics', 'observability-telemetry', 'robustness-fuzzing']\nCORE.JOBS.priorities | Priorities, QoS classes & latency-critical lanes | job-system-task-graph | E\nCORE.JOBS.hetero | Heterogeneous-core placement (P/E cores, SMT siblings) | job-system-task-graph | E | ['platform-architect']\nCORE.JOBS.numa | NUMA-aware scheduling | job-system-task-graph | E\nCORE.JOBS.completions | IO & GPU completion integration into the scheduler | job-system-task-graph | E | ['async-io-storage']\nCORE.JOBS.parallel-algos | Parallel-for & parallel algorithms | job-system-task-graph | E\nCORE.JOBS.blocking | Blocking & long-running task policy | job-system-task-graph | E\nCORE.JOBS.thread-model | Engine thread inventory (sole authority on which threads exist), core reservation, OS priority/QoS mapping, real-time thread rules, middleware pool adapters, oversubscription detection; forbidden-primitive lint for real-time threads | job-system-task-graph | E | ['platform-architect', 'audio-architect', 'cpu-performance']\nCORE.JOBS.pinned | Pinned-thread lanes for OS-thread-affine work | job-system-task-graph | E | ['platform-architect']\nCORE.JOBS.test-modes | Serial/deterministic execution mode & seeded schedule perturbation hooks | job-system-task-graph | E | ['robustness-fuzzing']\nCORE.JOBS.introspection | Task tracing, critical-path & utilization analysis, OS scheduler correlation | job-system-task-graph | E | ['observability-telemetry']\nCORE.JOBS.safety | Dependency-race detection for declared task dependencies | job-system-task-graph | E | ['robustness-fuzzing']\nCORE.JOBS.degenerate | Shipping inline/cooperative mode: the same task graph on 0–2 workers, no blocking waits on host threads, yield to the host event loop 